# The install media come in one edition per kind of graphics card, so each
# starts with the right driver settings and only the firmware it can use.
# NAME|KERNEL ARGUMENTS ADDED|FIRMWARE (all: every device's; nonvidia:
# everything but NVIDIA's, which is most of the image and of no use there)
#
# amd         Radeon RX 400 and newer, Radeon graphics in Ryzen processors
# amd-legacy  Radeon HD 2000 to HD 7000, R7 and R9: the amdgpu driver (Vulkan)
#             for GCN 1 and 2 cards, r600 and r300 OpenGL for older ones
# intel       Intel HD, UHD and Iris graphics (Core 2nd to 14th generation)
# intel-arc   Intel Arc cards and Core Ultra graphics, on the newer xe driver
# nvidia-rtx  GeForce RTX 20 to 50 and GTX 16: nouveau with NVIDIA's GSP
#             firmware (full clocks), NVK for Vulkan and Proton
# nvidia-gtx  GeForce GTX 10 and older: nouveau (NVIDIA doesn't let open
#             drivers raise these cards' clocks)
amd||nonvidia
amd-legacy|amdgpu.si_support=1 amdgpu.cik_support=1 radeon.si_support=0 radeon.cik_support=0|nonvidia
intel||nonvidia
intel-arc|i915.force_probe=!* xe.force_probe=*|nonvidia
nvidia-rtx|nouveau.config=NvGspRm=1|all
nvidia-gtx|nouveau.config=NvGspRm=0|all
